\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Environment and initial-state law}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}
\tag{reinforcement-learning}

\p{For a task #{q}, an \strong{environment} has a measurable hidden state
space #{\mathcal S_q}. Its \strong{initial-state law}
#{\mu_q\in\Delta(\mathcal S_q)} determines the state #{S_0} before the first
agent action.}

\p{This is the partially observable control model of
\citef{kaelbling1998planning}, specialized to a task-indexed finite-horizon
interaction. Hidden means that the policy does not receive #{S_t} directly.
The environment may reveal part of it through an observation.}

\p{The initial-state law is part of the experimental specification. Changing
it can change difficulty or leak task information even when the written prompt
is unchanged.}
